  "note": "Independent source rejudgment 2026-11-25 against RFC 9234 Section 5 (rfc/full/rfc9234.txt): \"If a route is to be advertised to a Customer, a Peer, or an RS-Client (when the sender is an RS), and the OTC Attribute is not present, then when advertising the route, an OTC Attribute MUST be added with a value equal to the AS number of the local AS.\" Verified all changes since 68d21a1c7f: all eight Go units (rfc9234_otc_procedures_test.go, rfc9234_otc_test.go) and checkOTCWithdrawal (internal/le/interoplab/bgp/check_rfc.go) are unchanged; b1eba99cf9/065e6e2d16 migrated role-otc-fwd-withdraw.ci, role-otc-rs-client-dest-stamp.ci, role-otc-rs-client-dest-stamp-forked.ci, and role-otc-rs-withdraw-eor.ci from plugin/attach blocks to bus (bgp-rib for forward/RS-client-dest tests with dest local IP 127.0.0.12 and NEXT_HOP 7F00000C, bgp-rs for RS withdraw/EoR), and 1f82b2727d reworded only the Linux-only netlink comment in the first three .ci files. All wire assertions remain intact: advertisements to Customer and RS-Client (both in-daemon and forked bgp-role) require exact OTC C023040000FDE8 (ASN 65000), while withdrawals and EoR require exact attribute-free frames (attrLen=0000). Verdict unchanged: enforced. Source rejudgment only; no test or gate executed.",
